1
00:00:02,386 --> 00:00:05,796
(Our Happy Days)

2
00:00:07,056 --> 00:00:09,026
(Yoon Jong Hoon, Uhm Hyun Kyung)

3
00:00:09,426 --> 00:00:10,896
(Jeong Yoon, Yoon Da Young)

4
00:00:12,366 --> 00:00:13,866
(Kim Hye Ok, Sunwoo Jae Duk)

5
00:00:13,866 --> 00:00:15,666
(Yoon Da Hoon, Moon Hee Kyung)

6
00:00:16,366 --> 00:00:18,506
(Lee Sang Sook, Jeong Ho Bin)

7
00:00:18,806 --> 00:00:20,676
(Lee Ho Jae, Jung Young Sook)

8
00:00:23,106 --> 00:00:24,346
(Choi Sung Won, Kim Soo Ah, Lee Da Eun)

9
00:00:24,746 --> 00:00:25,946
(Sung Byung Sook, Uhm Hye Soo)

10
00:00:26,216 --> 00:00:27,316
(Kim Na Ri, Yoo Jin Seok)

11
00:00:28,946 --> 00:00:30,986
(Ju Yong Man, Seo Dong Gyu, Jung Soo Ha, Jung Si Hyun)

12
00:00:33,674 --> 00:00:39,584
(Our Happy Days)

13
00:00:40,384 --> 00:00:41,854
(All characters, places, and organisations are fictional.)

14
00:00:41,854 --> 00:00:43,224
(Children and animals were filmed under production guidelines.)

15
00:00:44,854 --> 00:00:46,094
Listen carefully,

16
00:00:46,424 --> 00:00:47,594
both of you.

17
00:00:48,694 --> 00:00:51,824
I'm going to officially add Yeon Soon to our family.

18
00:00:53,264 --> 00:00:54,264
What?

19
00:00:54,634 --> 00:00:55,634
- Father. - Father.

20
00:00:56,164 --> 00:00:58,564
If you have a legitimate reason why I shouldn't, speak up.

21
00:00:59,374 --> 00:01:03,004
And cut the crap about her not being my flesh and blood.

22
00:01:03,344 --> 00:01:06,374
Father, as I've mentioned before...

23
00:01:06,674 --> 00:01:08,884
If she's added to the register,

24
00:01:08,944 --> 00:01:10,314
there will be issues with inheritance...

25
00:01:10,514 --> 00:01:12,114
and legal complications down the road.

26
00:01:12,714 --> 00:01:16,884
So that was why you hid this from me?

27
00:01:17,854 --> 00:01:19,224
Because you were afraid...

28
00:01:19,294 --> 00:01:21,754
your inheritance would shrink after I die?

29
00:01:24,624 --> 00:01:27,164
If that's what you're worried about, don't be. All right?

30
00:01:27,734 --> 00:01:29,564
As I've already declared,

31
00:01:30,804 --> 00:01:34,734
20 percent will be determined by the results of the competition.

32
00:01:35,504 --> 00:01:36,944
And as for the other 20 percent,

33
00:01:36,944 --> 00:01:38,374
you two should know all about that, shouldn't you?

34
00:01:40,514 --> 00:01:42,484
What do you mean, we should know?

35
00:01:42,484 --> 00:01:43,744
What are you talking about?

36
00:01:44,784 --> 00:01:46,614
You opened the safe.

37
00:01:47,184 --> 00:01:49,154
You must have read the will!

38
00:01:50,524 --> 00:01:54,124
- They opened the safe? - No, we didn't.

39
00:01:54,824 --> 00:01:57,624
I didn't see the will. I couldn't, Father.

40
00:01:57,794 --> 00:02:01,294
Are you trying to deny you opened the safe?

41
00:02:01,464 --> 00:02:02,764
No, that's not it...

42
00:02:03,434 --> 00:02:07,704
I did open it, but Min Ho suddenly walked in...

43
00:02:07,904 --> 00:02:10,504
Yes, Father. Min Ho came in...

44
00:02:10,574 --> 00:02:12,974
and said he'd disown us as his parents,

45
00:02:13,044 --> 00:02:14,344
so we just closed it.

46
00:02:14,644 --> 00:02:16,644
You must have a security camera installed,

47
00:02:16,644 --> 00:02:18,014
so feel free to check.

48
00:02:18,484 --> 00:02:20,684
We have nothing to hide. We swear...

49
00:02:21,084 --> 00:02:24,184
What? You'd swear to it?

50
00:02:26,854 --> 00:02:30,564
First, I'm going to ask Yeon Soon what she wants.

51
00:02:31,264 --> 00:02:32,764
Then I'll settle the issue with the family register.

52
00:02:33,534 --> 00:02:35,764
You ladies can wait outside.

53
00:02:36,404 --> 00:02:37,464
You stay, Dae Chi.

54
00:02:38,564 --> 00:02:39,604
Yes, Father.

55
00:02:47,274 --> 00:02:48,274
Goodness.

56
00:02:51,114 --> 00:02:54,314
Oh, for crying out loud. Seriously.

57
00:02:54,384 --> 00:02:57,684
What? What is it? Don't you say a word.

58
00:02:58,184 --> 00:02:59,994
Well, look who's getting defensive.

59
00:03:00,424 --> 00:03:03,064
I mean, if you don't cause trouble for one day,

60
00:03:03,124 --> 00:03:05,364
does it physically hurt you?

61
00:03:05,364 --> 00:03:07,094
- Mr. Ju! - Oh, dear.

62
00:03:08,594 --> 00:03:11,204
What? What's wrong?

63
00:03:11,364 --> 00:03:14,304
- Min Ho. - What is it now?

64
00:03:14,534 --> 00:03:17,204
Your father and I are completely screwed.

65
00:03:17,274 --> 00:03:18,744
We're left out in the cold.

66
00:03:19,014 --> 00:03:20,414
Grandfather's shares...

67
00:03:21,114 --> 00:03:22,114
I'm heading out.

68
00:03:22,844 --> 00:03:24,144
Hey, where are you going?

69
00:03:24,544 --> 00:03:26,384
Don't tell me you're going to see Seung Ri.

70
00:03:26,984 --> 00:03:29,454
No, don't go. I mean it.

71
00:03:32,454 --> 00:03:35,054
That heartless little jerk.

72
00:03:35,794 --> 00:03:39,494
Well, thank goodness...

73
00:03:39,864 --> 00:03:42,034
that you're nothing like your parents.

74
00:03:42,094 --> 00:03:43,234
I swear, you.

75
00:03:46,274 --> 00:03:47,574
Oh, my. Oh, my goodness.

76
00:03:49,744 --> 00:03:52,974
This is unbelievable.

77
00:03:54,144 --> 00:03:55,174
I,

78
00:03:55,714 --> 00:03:58,014
feeling like this was my last chance...

79
00:03:58,484 --> 00:04:00,054
and without your mother even knowing,

80
00:04:00,054 --> 00:04:02,154
was searching for Yeon Soon.

81
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:05,024
Your mother only recently...

82
00:04:05,454 --> 00:04:07,524
found out that I was looking for her again.

83
00:04:07,854 --> 00:04:10,124
So why couldn't you wait? Why?

84
00:04:12,664 --> 00:04:15,464
The reason I never told you...

85
00:04:15,904 --> 00:04:18,534
about your mother's daughter...

86
00:04:19,004 --> 00:04:20,634
is because I know you.

87
00:04:22,104 --> 00:04:25,814
I was worried you'd oppose it or get in the way.

88
00:04:27,214 --> 00:04:28,674
Father, what do you mean get in the way?

89
00:04:29,314 --> 00:04:31,684
No, if you had just told me from the start,

90
00:04:31,784 --> 00:04:33,454
I wouldn't have done what I did.

91
00:04:34,014 --> 00:04:37,554
Search your heart and be honest with yourself.

92
00:04:38,254 --> 00:04:40,824
Think about what you would've done if you'd known from the beginning.

93
00:04:44,124 --> 00:04:47,094
For the past 50 years,

94
00:04:47,634 --> 00:04:49,904
your mother raised you as more than her own son.

95
00:04:51,064 --> 00:04:53,404
Her final wish was to find her daughter,

96
00:04:54,774 --> 00:04:57,204
but you found her and hid that from us.

97
00:04:57,274 --> 00:05:00,374
How can you possibly expect me to forgive you? How?

98
00:05:01,514 --> 00:05:03,344
But even so,

99
00:05:03,844 --> 00:05:07,354
adding her to our family registry is going too far, Father.

100
00:05:08,414 --> 00:05:09,524
Ko Dae Chi.

101
00:05:10,454 --> 00:05:13,624
I don't have much time left.

102
00:05:15,024 --> 00:05:16,324
With you being the way you are,

103
00:05:17,124 --> 00:05:20,464
how am I supposed to rest in peace?

104
00:05:21,164 --> 00:05:22,164
Father.

105
00:05:22,904 --> 00:05:25,634
Why can't you understand how I feel? Why?

106
00:05:27,334 --> 00:05:28,534
Before I die,

107
00:05:29,474 --> 00:05:33,214
can't I see you act like a grown-up for once?

108
00:05:33,914 --> 00:05:34,914
Father,

109
00:05:35,614 --> 00:05:38,614
I really do want to earn your approval and be a good son.

110
00:05:39,014 --> 00:05:40,014
And...

111
00:05:40,454 --> 00:05:42,724
why do you keep talking about dying?

112
00:06:00,734 --> 00:06:01,734
Are you...

113
00:06:02,334 --> 00:06:04,144
on a hunger strike right now?

114
00:06:04,944 --> 00:06:08,414
Why haven't you eaten since last night? Why?

115
00:06:08,914 --> 00:06:11,084
I don't have time to eat right now.

116
00:06:11,444 --> 00:06:13,814
You're doing this because I said no to the studio, aren't you?

117
00:06:14,584 --> 00:06:16,284
- Is that it? - Yes, that's it.

118
00:06:17,654 --> 00:06:20,724
No, I told you it was a misunderstanding.

119
00:06:20,794 --> 00:06:22,964
Does this make any sense? Banning me from the studio...

120
00:06:23,024 --> 00:06:24,364
when I have a partner I'm working with?

121
00:06:24,424 --> 00:06:27,434
You can work separately, and if you need a meeting,

122
00:06:27,434 --> 00:06:29,964
you can just do a video call or whatever.

123
00:06:30,164 --> 00:06:32,934
You've always written just fine without a studio.

124
00:06:33,034 --> 00:06:35,204
Why are you so obsessed with having a studio now?

125
00:06:35,404 --> 00:06:37,374
What are you planning to do in a room...

126
00:06:37,444 --> 00:06:41,244
- with that pretty boy anyway? - Mom!

127
00:06:41,314 --> 00:06:42,344
I'm so disappointed.

128
00:06:42,884 --> 00:06:44,584
What? You're disappointed?

129
00:06:44,584 --> 00:06:46,584
Then why did you let me see something like that?

130
00:06:47,584 --> 00:06:48,754
My daughter is barely dressed...

131
00:06:48,814 --> 00:06:50,324
with her hair all wet, with some guy,

132
00:06:50,384 --> 00:06:53,094
what mother wouldn't be upset after seeing that?

133
00:06:53,154 --> 00:06:54,894
Who said I was barely dressed?

134
00:06:55,424 --> 00:06:57,464
Mom, are you really going to keep this up?

135
00:06:58,794 --> 00:07:02,264
If I can't release the webtoon on schedule,

136
00:07:02,334 --> 00:07:03,664
it's going to be all your fault.

137
00:07:06,074 --> 00:07:07,174
Fine, then,

138
00:07:07,974 --> 00:07:09,474
you'll have a curfew.

139
00:07:09,744 --> 00:07:10,744
A curfew?

140
00:07:11,244 --> 00:07:14,344
- You can't be serious. A curfew? - I am.

141
00:07:14,974 --> 00:07:18,914
No matter what, you have to be home by 11pm without fail.

142
00:07:19,214 --> 00:07:20,284
Or else...

143
00:07:20,984 --> 00:07:22,924
Is this really the 21st century?

144
00:07:23,184 --> 00:07:25,084
Did I travel back in time or something?

145
00:07:26,354 --> 00:07:28,024
I saw how cool you were...

146
00:07:28,024 --> 00:07:29,794
about Eun Ae and Team Leader Ko's relationship,

147
00:07:29,864 --> 00:07:32,064
so I thought you were really open-minded.

148
00:07:32,564 --> 00:07:35,094
But now I see you're not. You're completely old-fashioned.

149
00:07:35,464 --> 00:07:36,604
That's enough.

150
00:07:37,134 --> 00:07:38,764
If you promise to respect the curfew,

151
00:07:38,834 --> 00:07:40,574
you can go back to the studio next week.

152
00:07:40,874 --> 00:07:43,274
Why next week? Why can't I go today?

153
00:07:43,374 --> 00:07:47,074
We have a family meeting today, and we need to clean the house.

154
00:07:47,614 --> 00:07:50,944
And if you keep this up, I'll ban you from the studio again.

155
00:07:51,384 --> 00:07:54,284
Fine. You're so old-school.

156
00:07:54,684 --> 00:07:56,284
You're just figuring that out now?

157
00:07:56,854 --> 00:07:58,624
Anyway, where did Eun Ae go?

158
00:07:58,954 --> 00:08:01,894
I don't know. Probably out on a date with Team Leader Ko somewhere.

159
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:08,594
Weren't you with Eun Ae?

160
00:08:09,034 --> 00:08:10,864
No, isn't she in her room?

161
00:08:11,234 --> 00:08:12,334
I haven't seen her.

162
00:08:12,334 --> 00:08:15,204
I'm making ginseng chicken soup for lunch, so come down later.

163
00:08:15,274 --> 00:08:17,274
- Okay, I will. - Okay.

164
00:08:18,804 --> 00:08:19,974
Where on earth could she be?

165
00:08:25,284 --> 00:08:27,754
So, to keep Team Leader Ko from having nightmares,

166
00:08:27,814 --> 00:08:29,724
you made this by hand all night?

167
00:08:29,884 --> 00:08:32,694
Yes, but attaching these beads was so complicated...

168
00:08:32,754 --> 00:08:34,594
that I brought it to get your help.

169
00:08:36,694 --> 00:08:39,394
Ta-da. All done. It's finished.

170
00:08:40,994 --> 00:08:41,994
It's so pretty.

171
00:08:42,904 --> 00:08:44,464
They say sincerity can move mountains.

172
00:08:44,534 --> 00:08:45,964
He'll be so touched by your effort,

173
00:08:46,174 --> 00:08:49,404
- he won't have nightmares. - I really, really hope so.

174
00:08:52,304 --> 00:08:54,674
Yes, Team Leader Ko. Oh, I'm here with Cho Rong.

175
00:08:55,674 --> 00:08:56,944
Okay, I'll be right there.

176
00:08:57,884 --> 00:08:59,414
What? He wants you back right away?

177
00:09:00,084 --> 00:09:01,614
Can't he live a single moment without you?

178
00:09:01,684 --> 00:09:03,424
No, it's not like that.

179
00:09:03,724 --> 00:09:06,324
Oh, please. What do you mean it's not like that?

180
00:09:06,394 --> 00:09:09,124
You've only been here for an hour.

181
00:09:09,254 --> 00:09:12,794
He's acting like a husband tracking down his runaway wife.

182
00:09:12,864 --> 00:09:15,534
Tracking her down? No.

183
00:09:15,664 --> 00:09:17,734
It just means he's overflowing with love.

184
00:09:20,904 --> 00:09:24,744
Hey, Eun Ae. Love is important and all,

185
00:09:24,744 --> 00:09:27,174
but can't you do something for our Cho Rong?

186
00:09:27,244 --> 00:09:31,414
If there's a decent guy at your company, try to hook her up.

187
00:09:31,484 --> 00:09:33,684
Grandma, hook me up?

188
00:09:33,684 --> 00:09:35,084
I told you, I believe in natural encounters.

189
00:09:35,254 --> 00:09:37,824
You know, meeting someone naturally.

190
00:09:37,884 --> 00:09:40,424
Who are you fooling? A natural encounter, my foot.

191
00:09:40,854 --> 00:09:42,524
Okay, Grandma. I'll look for someone.

192
00:09:42,824 --> 00:09:45,864
- Cho Rong, I'm heading out. Thanks. - Okay, bye.

193
00:09:46,794 --> 00:09:49,864
What is that thing you made? A Dreamy?

194
00:09:50,004 --> 00:09:52,164
It's not a Dreamy, it's a dreamcatcher.

195
00:09:52,934 --> 00:09:54,534
I guess Team Leader Ko keeps having nightmares.

196
00:09:54,604 --> 00:09:58,674
My, and that round thing is supposed to stop nightmares?

197
00:09:58,804 --> 00:09:59,844
Yes.

198
00:09:59,844 --> 00:10:00,874
There.

199
00:10:03,514 --> 00:10:05,484
You made this yourself?

200
00:10:05,744 --> 00:10:07,954
Yes, I ordered the materials online...

201
00:10:07,954 --> 00:10:09,184
and worked on it from last night until now.

202
00:10:09,554 --> 00:10:12,054
Cho Rong helped me a bit with the beads.

203
00:10:13,454 --> 00:10:16,194
If you hang this up, bad dreams get caught in the web...

204
00:10:16,194 --> 00:10:17,724
and disappear with the morning sun,

205
00:10:17,824 --> 00:10:18,994
and only good dreams will come to you.

206
00:10:19,294 --> 00:10:21,494
Plus, my father personally carved this,

207
00:10:21,564 --> 00:10:23,304
so I attached this clover charm to it too.

208
00:10:23,734 --> 00:10:25,804
Don't you think you'll sleep soundly starting tonight?

209
00:10:26,674 --> 00:10:29,004
Thank you. And I'm sorry...

210
00:10:29,504 --> 00:10:32,344
- for making you worry. - What are you sorry for?

211
00:10:33,444 --> 00:10:35,114
My mom made ginseng chicken soup for lunch...

212
00:10:35,174 --> 00:10:36,444
and told us to come down quickly.

213
00:10:36,614 --> 00:10:39,144
Yes, time to recharge. Let's hurry down.

214
00:10:48,394 --> 00:10:50,964
You always prepare such a feast.

215
00:10:51,194 --> 00:10:53,734
- Thank you for the meal, Mother. - Of course, dig in.

216
00:10:54,034 --> 00:10:57,004
This clam soup is Seung Ri's creation.

217
00:10:57,164 --> 00:11:00,074
- What? Seung Ri made this? - Yes.

218
00:11:00,074 --> 00:11:01,604
Dad drank too much yesterday,

219
00:11:01,674 --> 00:11:03,204
so I made some hangover soup for him.

220
00:11:03,704 --> 00:11:07,674
- Dad, clams are good for hangovers. - Thanks, sweetie.

221
00:11:13,314 --> 00:11:14,314
How is it?

222
00:11:14,614 --> 00:11:17,124
It's good.

223
00:11:18,654 --> 00:11:20,154
I've lived to see the day.

224
00:11:20,554 --> 00:11:22,924
Our Seung Ri, who's never cooked anything...

225
00:11:22,924 --> 00:11:23,964
besides instant noodles,

226
00:11:24,524 --> 00:11:26,634
cooked a meal with her own hands because you were coming over.

227
00:11:27,234 --> 00:11:29,334
Mom, I told you it was hangover soup for Dad.

228
00:11:30,034 --> 00:11:33,604
- Will you stop the "Son-in-law Ko"? - Whatever.

229
00:11:33,904 --> 00:11:36,204
Well now, shall I try my daughter's cooking?

230
00:11:41,644 --> 00:11:45,384
So this is the dish made by Seo Seung Ri?

231
00:11:49,584 --> 00:11:52,654
Wait, wait, what is this? Did I just bite into sand?

232
00:11:55,024 --> 00:11:56,524
I think I broke a tooth.

233
00:11:56,894 --> 00:11:58,524
What are you going to do, Seo Seung Ri?

234
00:11:58,994 --> 00:11:59,994
Sand?

235
00:12:02,464 --> 00:12:03,804
You didn't clean the sand out of the clams?

236
00:12:04,164 --> 00:12:06,234
You insisted you could do it and didn't need help.

237
00:12:06,674 --> 00:12:08,634
Clean out the sand? I thought you just...

238
00:12:08,634 --> 00:12:10,044
washed the clams and put them in.

239
00:12:10,674 --> 00:12:12,544
Hold on. Let me try.

240
00:12:14,644 --> 00:12:19,384
It's refreshing. This is amazing.

241
00:12:20,284 --> 00:12:21,914
Hey, hey, hey, spit it out. Spit it out, come on.

242
00:12:21,984 --> 00:12:24,254
What, are you trying to chip a tooth and get an implant?

243
00:12:24,324 --> 00:12:26,254
- Come on, spit that out. - No, it's fine.

244
00:12:27,224 --> 00:12:29,024
What are you talking about? It's delicious.

245
00:12:29,664 --> 00:12:32,934
Delicious? It's salty as brine and full of sand.

246
00:12:33,194 --> 00:12:36,234
Well, if it's too salty, you can just add some water,

247
00:12:36,404 --> 00:12:38,734
and then you just take out the clam meat like this,

248
00:12:39,134 --> 00:12:40,734
and rinse it in the water before you eat it.

249
00:12:43,344 --> 00:12:46,044
This is the most delicious thing I've ever eaten in my life.

250
00:12:46,714 --> 00:12:51,214
Look, I know love is blind, but how can you possibly eat that?

251
00:12:52,014 --> 00:12:54,884
This is why Seo Seung Ri's behaviour is so bad. Ugh.

252
00:12:55,154 --> 00:12:56,754
Did you just say my behaviour is bad?

253
00:13:10,734 --> 00:13:12,934
They say you should strike while the iron is hot,

254
00:13:13,304 --> 00:13:15,304
so how about proposing to her again?

255
00:13:15,534 --> 00:13:18,444
Honey, can we please just eat in peace? Give it a rest.

256
00:13:18,644 --> 00:13:21,674
Do you really think I invited Min Ho over just to feed him?

257
00:13:22,414 --> 00:13:23,584
Oh, for goodness' sake.

258
00:13:25,284 --> 00:13:26,654
Sorry for interrupting the meal.

259
00:13:27,554 --> 00:13:29,624
Why are you eating this?

260
00:13:29,624 --> 00:13:31,154
Who are you going to blame when you get sick?

261
00:13:32,554 --> 00:13:34,694
What? Why? I think it tastes great.

262
00:13:35,224 --> 00:13:37,094
I got the saltiness just right, and she's taking it away.

263
00:13:39,124 --> 00:13:40,334
Hey, it's fine if you just add water.

264
00:13:41,034 --> 00:13:43,534
Doesn't Seo Seung Ri seem different somehow?

265
00:13:44,064 --> 00:13:45,604
It's so strange for her to just go out with Min Ho...

266
00:13:45,664 --> 00:13:46,674
because he asked.

267
00:13:46,974 --> 00:13:48,174
You think so too, don't you?

268
00:13:49,104 --> 00:13:52,004
It seems like a lot changed overnight.

269
00:13:52,304 --> 00:13:54,314
- Overnight? - Hey.

270
00:13:54,574 --> 00:13:56,014
Are you going to keep spouting nonsense?

271
00:13:56,074 --> 00:13:59,144
What's nonsensical about it? It's true that Seung Ri has changed.

272
00:13:59,614 --> 00:14:01,054
She used to throw a fit...

273
00:14:01,054 --> 00:14:02,554
if I even mentioned inviting Min Ho over,

274
00:14:02,754 --> 00:14:05,584
and now she's cooking for him and going on a date.

275
00:14:05,654 --> 00:14:07,824
Please, just don't jump to conclusions. Please.

276
00:14:10,464 --> 00:14:13,834
I should just get rid of his study.

277
00:14:14,864 --> 00:14:16,934
I wonder what he's got stashed in there.

278
00:14:17,534 --> 00:14:21,634
- I shall retire, Your Highness. - Seo Seung Woo.

279
00:14:22,304 --> 00:14:25,374
I'm the only one who's allowed to lay a hand on your back.

280
00:14:25,944 --> 00:14:28,774
Don't you dare get hit by anyone ever again.

281
00:14:31,184 --> 00:14:34,314
- What's got you in a good mood? - Of course I'm in a good mood.

282
00:14:35,314 --> 00:14:38,684
You used to not even let me suggest we get a meal together,

283
00:14:39,084 --> 00:14:41,824
but here you are, having a meal with me,

284
00:14:41,894 --> 00:14:44,724
and even agreeing to go on a date with me.

285
00:14:48,934 --> 00:14:51,734
There's something I want to ask you,

286
00:14:52,434 --> 00:14:54,274
about you preparing to study abroad...

287
00:14:55,274 --> 00:14:56,544
You still haven't given up on that?

288
00:14:56,644 --> 00:14:59,774
Yes. Why would I give up? Getting my MBA is my dream.

289
00:14:59,844 --> 00:15:03,284
But you said you accepted Gyeol and Jo Eun Ae's relationship.

290
00:15:04,084 --> 00:15:07,054
Are you still going abroad to follow Gyeol?

291
00:15:07,354 --> 00:15:08,614
My plans to study abroad have nothing to do...

292
00:15:08,614 --> 00:15:09,614
with Gyeol anymore.

293
00:15:10,184 --> 00:15:12,884
I just want to continue my studies for myself.

294
00:15:14,954 --> 00:15:16,664
I plan to take my time and prepare for it,

295
00:15:17,324 --> 00:15:19,394
and I'm thinking of looking into places other than New York.

296
00:15:19,794 --> 00:15:20,834
Oh, really?

297
00:15:21,194 --> 00:15:23,434
Well, in that case, I'll be your biggest supporter.

298
00:15:23,834 --> 00:15:25,764
Actually, maybe I should use this chance...

299
00:15:25,834 --> 00:15:27,574
to prepare to study abroad with you.

300
00:15:28,374 --> 00:15:30,174
General Director Ko Min Ho, aren't you going to prepare...

301
00:15:30,174 --> 00:15:31,444
for the third round of the competition?

302
00:15:31,544 --> 00:15:32,644
Right.

303
00:15:33,414 --> 00:15:35,414
We've got another fire to put out.

304
00:15:36,014 --> 00:15:37,014
Then...

305
00:15:37,514 --> 00:15:39,784
After Grandfather's living funeral is over,

306
00:15:40,484 --> 00:15:42,854
let's buckle down and get to it.

307
00:15:42,954 --> 00:15:45,254
Yes. I'm ready whenever you are.

308
00:15:46,724 --> 00:15:48,994
- Thank you, Seung Ri. - For what?

309
00:15:49,394 --> 00:15:51,124
If it weren't for you,

310
00:15:51,824 --> 00:15:54,464
I would've let my inferiority complex toward Gyeol...

311
00:15:54,994 --> 00:15:58,704
drive me to do anything to win this competition.

312
00:16:00,134 --> 00:16:01,474
But the reason I've changed...

313
00:16:02,134 --> 00:16:03,274
is all because of you.

314
00:16:04,104 --> 00:16:05,504
That in front of Seo Seung Ri,

315
00:16:07,074 --> 00:16:09,174
I can be someone who isn't the least bit shameful...

316
00:16:09,844 --> 00:16:11,314
and can become a better person.

317
00:16:12,584 --> 00:16:13,984
I tell myself that every day.

318
00:16:15,814 --> 00:16:16,824
So,

319
00:16:17,424 --> 00:16:18,424
thank you.

320
00:16:19,384 --> 00:16:20,424
No.

321
00:16:20,924 --> 00:16:22,224
It's not because of me.

322
00:16:23,464 --> 00:16:25,364
You're already a good person.

323
00:16:29,494 --> 00:16:30,504
Seung Ri.

324
00:16:36,004 --> 00:16:37,004
By the way,

325
00:16:37,444 --> 00:16:39,974
what are the plans for the Chairman's living funeral?

326
00:16:40,144 --> 00:16:44,344
I don't have any specific plans yet. I have to start thinking about it.

327
00:16:44,614 --> 00:16:47,614
I'll sort it out and submit a proposal by tomorrow.

328
00:16:48,014 --> 00:16:50,384
You really are the brains of the Planning Team.

329
00:16:51,484 --> 00:16:52,984
You're busy, so we should get going.

330
00:16:53,624 --> 00:16:54,794
Right, let's go.

331
00:17:01,994 --> 00:17:04,934
Gosh that bench... My father bought the wood...

332
00:17:04,934 --> 00:17:06,464
and spent three days making that bench.

333
00:17:06,534 --> 00:17:09,774
What? Your father made this himself?

334
00:17:10,504 --> 00:17:13,514
It didn't look hard online making furniture like this,

335
00:17:13,514 --> 00:17:14,544
so I gave it a shot,

336
00:17:15,014 --> 00:17:16,314
but it gave me a lot of trouble.

337
00:17:16,984 --> 00:17:19,744
But it's held up well for ten years.

338
00:17:21,314 --> 00:17:23,114
- All done. - Okay.

339
00:17:23,724 --> 00:17:26,384
- All right, come have watermelon. - Okay.

340
00:17:26,384 --> 00:17:28,394
- You too, Bit Na. - Yes, Grandma.

341
00:17:30,494 --> 00:17:31,594
Thanks to our Bit Na,

342
00:17:31,664 --> 00:17:33,864
the flowers are getting a nice cool drink.

343
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:39,834
But why haven't we seen Eun Nim at all?

344
00:17:40,174 --> 00:17:41,804
She even said she wouldn't eat the ginseng chicken soup.

345
00:17:42,104 --> 00:17:44,904
She's mad at me. And she's busy right now.

346
00:17:45,144 --> 00:17:46,744
Why? Did something happen?

347
00:17:47,144 --> 00:17:48,944
I don't know. I'll tell you later.

348
00:17:49,944 --> 00:17:51,584
Ginseng chicken soup and watermelon...

349
00:17:51,644 --> 00:17:52,744
I'm really set for summer.

350
00:17:53,754 --> 00:17:56,454
Father, shall we go to the mineral spring? It's been a while.

351
00:17:56,514 --> 00:17:57,954
We can stop by the bathhouse on the way down.

352
00:17:58,024 --> 00:18:01,994
A bathhouse in this sweltering heat? I'm sweating just sitting still.

353
00:18:02,054 --> 00:18:04,394
No, don't you know you have to fight fire with fire?

354
00:18:04,794 --> 00:18:08,394
Before Eun Hyung got married, we went every single weekend.

355
00:18:09,364 --> 00:18:12,134
We're all done with work. Should we go now?

356
00:18:12,234 --> 00:18:14,074
Yes, I'll get ready and be right out.

357
00:18:16,534 --> 00:18:20,114
- Team Leader Ko, get ready quickly. - Yes? Me too?

358
00:18:20,614 --> 00:18:22,074
Of course you have to come.

359
00:18:22,144 --> 00:18:24,514
It's a tradition for the men in this family.

360
00:18:24,714 --> 00:18:27,384
Going to the bathhouse on a day off to scrub each other's backs.

361
00:18:28,514 --> 00:18:30,954
But what do I need to prepare?

362
00:18:31,224 --> 00:18:34,294
Just bring a change of underwear. Everything else is at the bathhouse.

363
00:18:35,054 --> 00:18:36,394
- Have you... - Yes?

364
00:18:36,454 --> 00:18:37,824
never been to a public bathhouse?

365
00:18:39,024 --> 00:18:40,694
A few times when I was little, with my father...

366
00:18:41,094 --> 00:18:42,894
My biological father, who passed away.

367
00:18:45,104 --> 00:18:46,434
I see.

368
00:18:47,104 --> 00:18:50,104
- I'll get ready and be right out. - I have to use the bathroom.

369
00:18:50,174 --> 00:18:52,304
- Okay. - I'll get ready and be out, too.

370
00:18:52,304 --> 00:18:53,544
Okay.

371
00:18:55,174 --> 00:18:57,784
He seems so happy they invited him to the bathhouse.

372
00:18:58,684 --> 00:19:00,284
How old was he when his biological father died,

373
00:19:00,354 --> 00:19:02,614
- and how did it happen? - I don't know the details.

374
00:19:02,684 --> 00:19:04,524
Just that when Team Leader Ko was seven,

375
00:19:04,584 --> 00:19:06,224
he died in an accident...

376
00:19:07,224 --> 00:19:09,054
Don't ask him until he brings it up himself.

377
00:19:09,624 --> 00:19:11,394
You don't want to open up old wounds.

378
00:19:13,994 --> 00:19:15,094
Honey,

379
00:19:15,494 --> 00:19:16,764
do you think Father will really put Kang Yeon Ja...

380
00:19:16,834 --> 00:19:17,834
on the family register?

381
00:19:19,334 --> 00:19:21,404
Have you ever known Father to make empty promises?

382
00:19:23,404 --> 00:19:26,074
Why did you have to slip up about something that's in the past?

383
00:19:27,074 --> 00:19:28,374
Tell me about it.

384
00:19:28,914 --> 00:19:30,684
Why am I like this?

385
00:19:30,684 --> 00:19:33,184
I can't keep a poker face or watch what I say.

386
00:19:35,154 --> 00:19:36,214
Gosh.

387
00:19:37,354 --> 00:19:40,424
By the way, Father asked you to stay behind earlier.

388
00:19:40,754 --> 00:19:42,054
What did you talk about?

389
00:19:42,924 --> 00:19:44,194
What do you think? It was about Mother.

390
00:19:44,994 --> 00:19:47,964
He said she raised me like her own son for 50 years,

391
00:19:48,034 --> 00:19:50,404
so how could I get in the way of her finding her daughter?

392
00:19:50,704 --> 00:19:52,064
He told me to grow up.

393
00:19:52,134 --> 00:19:54,834
So, are you feeling remorseful now?

394
00:19:55,704 --> 00:19:58,644
Father's being so firm about it. What choice do I have?

395
00:19:59,044 --> 00:20:00,174
If I can't be remorseful,

396
00:20:00,814 --> 00:20:02,274
I at least have to pretend to be.

397
00:20:02,514 --> 00:20:06,384
Honey, if you think about it, we didn't do anything that wrong.

398
00:20:06,784 --> 00:20:08,614
Don't you know the saying about human relations?

399
00:20:08,614 --> 00:20:12,424
I mean, wouldn't anyone feel the same way?

400
00:20:13,224 --> 00:20:15,654
The saying is "human nature."

401
00:20:15,724 --> 00:20:19,494
Oh, please. You knew what I meant.

402
00:20:19,964 --> 00:20:22,964
And don't get ahead of yourself worrying, all right?

403
00:20:23,464 --> 00:20:26,034
Putting her on the family registry is Father's idea,

404
00:20:26,034 --> 00:20:27,704
not necessarily hers.

405
00:20:28,874 --> 00:20:31,344
Are you saying that Kang Yeon Ja might actually refuse?

406
00:20:31,474 --> 00:20:33,744
Yes, that's exactly what I'm saying.

407
00:20:34,344 --> 00:20:38,744
Crystal. If it were you, could you turn down that offer?

408
00:20:39,414 --> 00:20:42,154
To become the daughter of the Gangsu Group's Chairman overnight,

409
00:20:42,214 --> 00:20:44,524
with full legal and social recognition.

410
00:20:45,324 --> 00:20:47,594
Me? If it were me, I'd obviously...

411
00:20:49,094 --> 00:20:50,524
refuse.

412
00:20:50,864 --> 00:20:53,734
Oh, what do we do if she accepts on the spot?

413
00:20:55,534 --> 00:20:57,864
Working up a good sweat feels so refreshing.

414
00:20:59,104 --> 00:21:01,674
Eun Hyung, I heard you had a nosebleed.

415
00:21:02,104 --> 00:21:03,844
Gosh, Mother...

416
00:21:04,204 --> 00:21:06,814
I specifically begged her not to tell you.

417
00:21:07,614 --> 00:21:09,574
I understand your intentions,

418
00:21:10,114 --> 00:21:11,244
but you have to give one of them up.

419
00:21:11,584 --> 00:21:13,284
Your body doesn't lie.

420
00:21:14,254 --> 00:21:16,854
You need to think about the long haul in everything you do.

421
00:21:17,424 --> 00:21:19,024
Do you really think your life will change...

422
00:21:19,024 --> 00:21:20,294
if you make money by working nonstop?

423
00:21:21,024 --> 00:21:22,454
You have to think of Bit Na.

424
00:21:23,054 --> 00:21:25,324
Yes, I understand what you're saying.

425
00:21:26,794 --> 00:21:28,334
That goes for you too, Team Leader Ko.

426
00:21:28,834 --> 00:21:30,364
I saw the video from the competition,

427
00:21:30,434 --> 00:21:32,064
and you looked like you were struggling.

428
00:21:32,434 --> 00:21:34,604
Yes, to be honest, I haven't been well,

429
00:21:34,874 --> 00:21:37,144
but I'm trying my best to get better.

430
00:21:37,944 --> 00:21:40,774
Don't try to carry every burden by yourself.

431
00:21:41,144 --> 00:21:42,474
If you're struggling, say you're struggling.

432
00:21:42,744 --> 00:21:44,084
If you're in pain, say you're in pain.

433
00:21:44,644 --> 00:21:46,614
When you share good things, they double,

434
00:21:46,684 --> 00:21:49,914
and when you share bad things, they're cut in half.

435
00:21:50,554 --> 00:21:51,784
You know what I mean, right?

436
00:21:52,254 --> 00:21:53,254
Yes.

437
00:21:55,954 --> 00:21:57,024
Why are you looking at me like that?

438
00:21:58,024 --> 00:21:59,294
Thank you, Father.

439
00:22:05,234 --> 00:22:06,264
Yes, Chairman.

440
00:22:07,374 --> 00:22:08,534
This evening?

441
00:22:10,104 --> 00:22:12,744
Yes, I understand. I'll see you then.

442
00:22:13,614 --> 00:22:14,744
Was that my grandfather?

443
00:22:15,474 --> 00:22:19,144
Yes. He wants me and Yeon Ja to come to the house tonight.

444
00:22:20,554 --> 00:22:21,814
I wonder what it's about.

445
00:22:24,854 --> 00:22:26,994
What? The family registry?

446
00:22:27,594 --> 00:22:30,424
Now that the family head system has been abolished,

447
00:22:30,494 --> 00:22:31,664
it might not mean much,

448
00:22:32,894 --> 00:22:35,734
but I want to make it official that you're our child,

449
00:22:36,764 --> 00:22:39,104
at least on paper.

450
00:22:41,004 --> 00:22:43,944
I haven't really thought about that.

451
00:22:45,374 --> 00:22:47,844
Just finding my mother is enough for me.

452
00:22:48,014 --> 00:22:50,144
That may be true,

453
00:22:51,084 --> 00:22:54,214
but why don't you think it over some more?

454
00:22:56,984 --> 00:22:59,454
What do you think? Do you feel the same way?

455
00:23:00,554 --> 00:23:03,254
Yes, I feel the same way she does, Chairman.

456
00:23:03,694 --> 00:23:07,034
It's enough for us to live our lives with you as our parents.

457
00:23:07,634 --> 00:23:09,994
What does a silly piece of paper matter?

458
00:23:11,804 --> 00:23:13,204
No, it's not that.

459
00:23:13,674 --> 00:23:14,834
It's just that after Yeon Soon was separated from us,

460
00:23:14,834 --> 00:23:18,744
she moved from place to place, not knowing where her roots were,

461
00:23:19,544 --> 00:23:23,914
unable to live with her feet firmly on the ground.

462
00:23:24,214 --> 00:23:25,814
That's what breaks my heart.

463
00:23:28,054 --> 00:23:30,254
Yes, I understand what you're saying.

464
00:23:31,224 --> 00:23:32,224
I'll...

465
00:23:33,284 --> 00:23:35,794
think about it carefully and get back to you.

466
00:23:36,554 --> 00:23:38,664
All right. Do that.

467
00:23:40,364 --> 00:23:43,364
I'd like to see the grandkids sometime,

468
00:23:44,164 --> 00:23:47,174
but I haven't had a chance to talk to anyone but Eun Ae.

469
00:23:47,704 --> 00:23:50,574
Before your father's living funeral,

470
00:23:50,874 --> 00:23:53,274
if you have the time, please bring them over.

471
00:23:53,744 --> 00:23:56,214
I just want to at least cook a meal for them.

472
00:23:57,214 --> 00:23:58,584
Yes, I will, Mother.

473
00:24:07,254 --> 00:24:09,024
(Yugwang Apartment Complex Construction Site)

474
00:24:20,404 --> 00:24:22,534
He's the spitting image of his father.

475
00:24:23,804 --> 00:24:25,704
So you're Gyeol.

476
00:24:27,814 --> 00:24:31,484
I'm the president of the company your father worked for.

477
00:24:32,314 --> 00:24:33,314
How old are you?

478
00:24:33,914 --> 00:24:35,454
He can't talk.

479
00:24:36,814 --> 00:24:37,824
Excuse me?

480
00:24:38,554 --> 00:24:40,824
It's because he saw what happened to his dad right in front of him.

481
00:24:41,524 --> 00:24:44,794
- He's been silent since that day. - Excuse me.

482
00:24:45,764 --> 00:24:46,794
- Just a moment. - Okay.

483
00:24:57,704 --> 00:25:01,274
Your father was a truly wonderful man.

484
00:25:02,374 --> 00:25:03,414
Your father...

485
00:25:04,614 --> 00:25:06,714
will be watching over you from paradise.

486
00:25:08,114 --> 00:25:09,114
So...

487
00:25:10,114 --> 00:25:11,284
Oh, dear...

488
00:25:11,624 --> 00:25:13,054
How could he rest, with that child lingering in his thoughts?

489
00:25:13,484 --> 00:25:15,424
How could he have died peacefully?

490
00:25:17,294 --> 00:25:18,894
Oh, our Manager Han.

491
00:25:21,264 --> 00:25:22,694
Yes, Secretary Ju.

492
00:25:23,704 --> 00:25:25,234
Why didn't I think of that until now?

493
00:25:30,074 --> 00:25:33,674
What? You want me to trace the finance team's cash flow?

494
00:25:34,214 --> 00:25:37,714
Yes, I've been keeping an eye on it.

495
00:25:37,984 --> 00:25:39,184
Something's going on.

496
00:25:40,914 --> 00:25:43,754
And discreetly look into the relationship...

497
00:25:43,754 --> 00:25:45,384
between President Ko and the finance director.

498
00:25:46,084 --> 00:25:47,154
Yes.

499
00:25:49,494 --> 00:25:53,394
By any chance, do you have anything to tell me about the CFO?

500
00:25:55,634 --> 00:25:57,264
The Finance Director? Why do you ask?

501
00:25:57,804 --> 00:26:00,134
It seems he's very close with the President,

502
00:26:00,434 --> 00:26:02,504
so I was wondering if there was anything I should know.

503
00:26:04,204 --> 00:26:07,214
Yes, I feel bad asking this of you.

504
00:26:08,714 --> 00:26:11,814
Making you dig into my own son's faults...

505
00:26:12,544 --> 00:26:13,544
Not at all, sir.

506
00:26:14,414 --> 00:26:16,214
I'll look into it and report back to you.

507
00:26:17,354 --> 00:26:18,354
I'll be on my way.

508
00:26:24,594 --> 00:26:26,724
- Sir. - Oh, Gyeol.

509
00:26:27,534 --> 00:26:28,534
Goodness.

510
00:26:29,494 --> 00:26:32,304
What brings you here so early? Are you here to see the Chairman?

511
00:26:32,364 --> 00:26:34,204
No, I came to see you, sir.

512
00:26:34,534 --> 00:26:36,334
Me? Why me?

513
00:26:37,174 --> 00:26:40,414
You came to my father's funeral 25 years ago, didn't you?

514
00:26:40,474 --> 00:26:44,344
What? Oh, yes. I went with the Chairman.

515
00:26:44,584 --> 00:26:46,144
But why bring that up all of a sudden?

516
00:26:46,514 --> 00:26:48,854
Thank you so much for coming back then.

517
00:26:49,714 --> 00:26:52,854
I was so young, I'd forgotten about it for a while.

518
00:26:52,954 --> 00:26:55,124
Oh, don't mention it.

519
00:26:56,354 --> 00:27:00,964
You were in such shock that you couldn't speak for a while.

520
00:27:02,494 --> 00:27:06,904
But I doubt you came here this early just to say thanks.

521
00:27:07,004 --> 00:27:11,744
You're right. Do you happen to know anything about my father's accident?

522
00:27:11,804 --> 00:27:14,614
What kind of accident it was and how it happened...

523
00:27:15,544 --> 00:27:19,084
Well, all I know is that it was a car accident.

524
00:27:20,184 --> 00:27:25,524
At night, a speeding car tried to pass your father's car and...

525
00:27:26,254 --> 00:27:27,254
What?

526
00:27:30,664 --> 00:27:31,664
Chief Seo.

527
00:27:59,154 --> 00:28:02,024
(Our Happy Days)

528
00:28:02,254 --> 00:28:05,294
- Happy Kiss Day. - Wait a minute.

529
00:28:06,164 --> 00:28:08,334
Hye Ji, this is a complete misunderstanding.

530
00:28:08,434 --> 00:28:10,064
Is this because of Eun Nim?

531
00:28:10,134 --> 00:28:12,534
Since it's come to this, I'll make my intentions clear.

532
00:28:12,534 --> 00:28:14,204
I like you, Eun Nim.

533
00:28:14,534 --> 00:28:16,404
I told my dad on my birthday...

534
00:28:16,534 --> 00:28:18,674
that I wanted to live happily ever after...

535
00:28:18,744 --> 00:28:20,674
with my dad until the end of the world.

536
00:28:20,874 --> 00:28:24,044
I'll always be by your side, Team Leader Ko.

537
00:28:24,114 --> 00:28:28,714
Will you stay with me until the end of the world?

538
00:28:34,794 --> 00:28:39,194
(Our Happy Days)
